Why: Balance2Way() passes a real_t expression to iabs(), i.e. abs() of
 int, which clang reports (-Wabsolute-value, a significant warning for
 R CMD check). The conversion to idx_t is now explicit; the behavior
 (truncation, then absolute value) is unchanged. Later METIS releases use
 rabs() here instead, which would change orderings slightly.
Upstream: fixed differently in METIS 5.1.1+ (rabs).
Obsolete when: METIS is updated.

